<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32645" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏnychĭnus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνύχινος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of the color of the finger-nail</i>, <i>nail-colored</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pira,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 15, 16, § 55</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pruna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					12, 10</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Of the marble called</i> onyx: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lapis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Gen. 2, 12</span></i>
			.—As <i>subst.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">onychinus,</span>”
				<i>the onyx</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Exod. 39, 13</span></i>
			.—<b>Transf.</b>, <i>resembling the onyx</i> (<b>poet.</b>) of the
			coating of ice on rivers: tegimen onychinum, Laev ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 19, 7</span></i>
			<i>fin.—Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏnychĭna</span></b>  (sc.
			vasa), n.
			plur., <i>vessels of onyx</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Lampr. Heliog. 32</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
